   "notes": "36 simulated patients in three arms of a blood-pressure trial. Group and Sex are text (categorical) variables: they hold words, shown left-aligned and marked “abc” in the header. BMI, Change, Obese and Treated are calculated variables (ƒx): select one to see its formula in the bar above the grid. They update as soon as a value they use changes; try editing a weight, or a follow-up blood pressure. Two follow-up visits were missed, so their Change is empty. The bubble plot is coloured by Group (a text variable: one colour per category). “Change by group” was made with Extract and rearrange (Change split by the categories of Group) and is analyzed by a one-way ANOVA; the multiple regression uses the calculated BMI and Treated as predictors."
